type: software
title: "equivtest: equivalence testing and run-count design for stochastic machine-learning experiments"
authors:
  - family-names: Knopov
    given-names: Dmytro
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-9958-5793"
    affiliation: "National University of Kyiv-Mohyla Academy"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-16
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DmytroKnopov/equivtest"
abstract: "Seed-level Welch-TOST for the practical equivalence of two training methods, a two-level (seed x item) hierarchical bootstrap, and a power analysis giving the number of training runs that a certification at a given margin requires, with the exact pooled-model TOST power as a benchmark. Companion code, simulation studies and case-study data for the article 'Equivalence testing and run-count design for stochastic machine-learning experiments' (D. Knopov and N. Shvai, 2026)."
keywords:
  - equivalence testing
  - statistical power
  - experimental design
  - hierarchical bootstrap
  - machine learning
